2026-06-30 14:57:51,391 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'timeout': 300, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-bf004bcc-6d79-47b7-bcaa-75481b1f7d94', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are an expert SDRF-Proteomics annotator for crosslinking mass spectrometry (XL-MS) datasets.\n\nExtract the following SDRF metadata terms from the provided publication text and/or PRIDE project description.\n\nTERMS TO EXTRACT:\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nterm: sex\nsdrf_column: characteristics[sex]\nontology: PATO:0000047\ndescription: Biological sex of the donor.\nallowed_values: male, female, intersex, hermaphrodite, anonymized, not available, not applicable\ninstructions: Use one of the fixed values above. Return "not available" if not stated.\n  Return "not applicable" if the sample is from a cell line or organism without defined sex.\n\nterm: age\nsdrf_column: characteristics[age]\nontology: EFO:0000246\ndescription: Age of the donor at sample collection.\npattern: {Number}{Unit} where Unit is Y (years), M (months), W (weeks), D (days).\n  Also allowed: "anonymized" if age is stated but anonymized.\ninstructions: Return null if not stated.\n\nterm: ancestry category\nsdrf_column: characteristics[ancestry category]\nontology: HANCESTRO\ndescription: Ancestry or ethnic background of the donor.\ninstructions: Use HANCESTRO terms if possible. Return null if not stated or not applicable.\n\nterm: biological replicate\nsdrf_column: characteristics[biological replicate]\nontology: MS:1001809\ndescription: Identifier for the biological replicate (integer or "pooled").\ninstructions: Return a description of the replication strategy from the paper\n  (e.g. "3 biological replicates", "2 independent experiments"). The actual\n  integer values are assigned per-file automatically; describe what you find in the text.\n\nterm: genotype\nsdrf_column: characteristics[genotype]\nontology: EFO:0000513\ndescription: Known genetic variant, mutation, or genotype of the subject.\ninstructions: Return null if not stated. Example: "wild type", "Δatg5", "ΔYme1".\n\nterm: pooled sample\nsdrf_column: characteristics[pooled sample]\nontology: NCIT:C165587\ndescription: Whether the sample is a pooled sample.\nallowed_values: not pooled, pooled, or pattern SN=sample1;SN=sample2\ninstructions: Return "not pooled" unless explicitly stated otherwise.\n\nterm: phosphate\nsdrf_column: characteristics[phosphate]\nontology: PRIDE:0000805\ndescription: Phosphate concentration (only relevant for environmental/water samples).\npattern: number + mg/L or umol/L\ninstructions: Return null unless this is a water/environmental sample with explicit\n  phosphate concentration stated.\n\nterm: temperature\nsdrf_column: characteristics[temperature]\nontology: PRIDE:0000703\ndescription: Temperature at the sampling location (environmental samples only).\npattern: number + °C\ninstructions: Return null unless this is an environmental/metaproteomics sample\n  with explicit temperature stated. Do NOT confuse with crosslinking temperature.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nReturn a single JSON object where each key is the exact sdrf_column string shown above.\nFor each key, return a dict with:\n  "value": the extracted value (string, list, or null)\n  "accession": ontology accession if resolvable, else null\n  "confidence": "high", "medium", or "low"\n  "evidence_quote": short verbatim quote from the text, or null\n  "evidence_location": location in the paper (e.g. "Methods"), or null'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '[TITLE]\nCross-linking/mass spectrometry analysis of the AOC complex\n\n[ABSTRACT]\nAs a part of a study on how kinetochors are assembled at the centromeres of the chromosomes, cross-linking/mass spectrometry has been applied to investigate interactions between Okp1/ Ame1 heterodimer, which is part of the COMA complex,  and CENP-A from Saccharomyces cerevisiae.\n\n[METHODS]\nThe purified Ame1/Okp1/Cse4N complex at a concentration of 1.2 mg/ml was crosslinked with 150 μM BS3 (bis(sulfosuccinimidyl) suberate) in 50 mM HEPES, pH 7.5, 200 mM NaCl and 1 mM DTT and incubated for 2 h on ice. The reaction was stopped with 50 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5, and proteins were separated by SDS-PAGE electrophoresis. A gel band corresponding to the monomeric cross-linked Ame1/Okp1/Cse4N complex was excised from the gel and digested with trypsin (Pierce, Germany) (Shevchenko et al., 2006). The resulting tryptic peptides were extracted from the gel de-salted using C18 StageTips (Rappsilber et al., 2003).  LC-MS/MS analysis was conducted in triplicates, performed on an Orbitrap FusionTM LumosTM TribridTM mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific, Germany) coupled on-line to Ultimate 3000 RSLCano Systems (Dionex, Thermo Fisher Scientific, Germany). The eluted peptides are ionized by an EASY-Spray source (Thermo Scientific). Mobile phase A consists of water, 0.1% v/v formic acid and mobile phase B consists of 80% v/v acetonitrile and 0.1% v/v formic acid. For CLMS analysis, peptides are loaded at a flow-rate of 0.3 μL/min and eluted at 0.2 μL/min using a linear gradient going from 2% mobile phase B to 40% mobile phase B over 139 min, followed by a linear increase from 45% to 95% mobile phase B in twelve min. The MS data is acquired in the data-dependent mode with the top-speed option. For each three-second acquisition cycle, the full scan mass spectrum was recorded in the Orbitrap with a resolution of 120,000. The ions with a precursor charge state between 3+ and 7+ were isolated and fragmented. Each cross-linked sample was analysed with two LC-MS/MS acquisitions, in one acquisition, peptides were fragmented using Higher-energy collisional dissociation (HCD) with 30% collision energy. The fragmentation spectra were then recorded in the Orbitrap with a resolution of 30000. Dynamic exclusion was enabled with single repeat count and 60-second exclusion duration.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
